 "content": "# Continual-ARC note: marker counts in separator tiles

A demonstrated ARC pattern used full-width/full-height separator lines to divide a grid into equal tiles; the output had one cell per tile. Counting the standout marker (color 6) inside each 3×3 tile matched the demo: tiles with 2 markers mapped to 1, while tiles with 1 marker mapped to the tile/background color (8). A separate solved test with 2×2 tiles likewise mapped tiles with at least 2 marker cells (color 9) to 1 and tiles with one marker to the background color (2).

